    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d707">

                <pb facs="0845" n="829" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.504 Mexico/10–1647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-16T19:00:00-06:00">October 16, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1124. Embassy today received Foreign Office note 34231 October 15<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d707-f1"/> referring supplementary agreement for contracting workers
                    in Texas signed January 31 confirmed in exchange of notes of March 10, 1947
                        (Embsdes 3090 March 14<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d707-f2"/>) and stating that in view fact that as regards Mexican
                    workers in Texas stimulation [<hi rendition="#italic">stipulations?</hi>] of
                    general agreement have not been fulfilled at least to desired extent and taking
                    account hopes not realized favorably for solving discrimination against Mexicans
                    in Texas. Mexican Government resolved terminate supplementary agreement and
                    consequently will no longer authorize contracts Mexican laborers found illegally
                    in Texas. Copy and translation note being forwarded by pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
